---
description: Document and enforce typed object literal patterns for safer TS code.
globs: '**/*.ts,**/*.tsx'
alwaysApply: true
---

Type object literals explicitly when declaring or returning them.

## Examples

- Variable:

  - Avoid: `const value = { id: 1 }`
  - Prefer: `const value: MyType = { id: 1 }`

- Arrow return:

  - Avoid: `items.map((item) => ({ id: item.id }))`
  - Prefer: `items.map((item): MyType => ({ id: item.id }))`

- Function return:
  - Avoid: `function build() { return { id: 1 }; }`
  - Prefer: `function build(): MyType { return { id: 1 }; }`

Use a narrow inline type if it is local-only; avoid `any`.
